    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "First, solve for $x$ in the given equation $2x+7=3$.\n\nStep 1: Subtract 7 from both sides of the equation.\n\\[2x + 7 - 7 = 3 - 7\\]\n\\[2x = -4\\]\n\nStep 2: Divide both sides by 2.\n\\[x = \\frac{-4}{2}\\]\n\\[x = -2\\]\n\nNow, we know that the solution $x = -2$ is common to both equations. Next, substitute $x = -2$ into the second equation $bx-10=-2$ to solve for $b$.\n\nStep 3: Substitute $x = -2$ into the second equation.\n\\[b(-2) - 10 = -2\\]\n\nStep 4: Simplify the equation.\n\\[-2b - 10 = -2\\]\n\nStep 5: Add 10 to both sides of the equation.\n\\[-2b - 10 + 10 = -2 + 10\\]\n\\[-2b = 8\\]\n\nStep 6: Divide both sides by -2 to solve for $b$.\n\\[b = \\frac{8}{-2}\\]\n\\[b = -4\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of $b$ is $\\boxed{-4}$.",
